{
  "slug": "clinical-rating-scales-and-outcome-measures-mds-updrs",
  "concept": "Clinical rating scales and outcome measures: MDS-UPDRS",
  "generated": "2026-11-27",
  "summary": "Source-anchored research for Clinical rating scales and outcome measures: MDS-UPDRS. Run status: COMPLETED.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Structure and components",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "MDS-UPDRS assesses four domains: Part I non-motor experiences of daily living, Part II motor experiences of daily living, Part III motor examination, and Part IV motor complications; it is used in clinical care and research. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19025984/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:dd7c73f93f931b0aaa05c963160d61b534cd3813850741a5dcadafa550b97d83",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4b46a1e0e2e0101b80cfbf9ad16cd0534a3d8ba2aae5d5e89a059da1f067d252",
            "ev:57be0954b43e2e6d83fee056b332151452fab917370d24d6339120b3b92297e7"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.movementdisorders.org/MDS/MDS-Rating-Scales/MDS-Unified-Parkinsons-Disease-Rating-Scale-MDS-UPDRS.htm"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The original MDS-UPDRS clinimetric study tested 877 patients at 39 sites and found internal consistency of 0.79–0.93 across parts; factor analyses supported separate part sum scores in preference to an all-parts total. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19025984/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6e101b4093b6a995c8ca537a068f60bb2612e32486a0356782c7792b63bcbfe5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b44ef4994e2aca127557755cce1a0877231f1eb9198df1f807c075c24485c635",
            "ev:b91e9513968c0d37906f98d36b2d92c593ac0aacf8ccf77efba2b229177436ca",
            "ev:e7e5c2ba382957740fe9ecd3ec10da033c2c2fed2b1f819e8901c48e361ea6f1",
            "ev:f39c19994d91cb1886c6f2e2e90338261edbb55cef3a8d4f8968450929ae5057"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "An independent Spanish-language validation in 435 patients reported intraclass correlation above 0.85 for each part total, while noting a moderate floor effect (30 %) for Part IV. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22865238/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:36d76d85a70373ecc42a876728314d83b87d2a1543906e87dd0d83791c965209",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:918ed8272b49f5cb7dab07e6640069dfdc93b7ce1ad016c42766b432aa0d6b93",
            "ev:94edd3a35d7b3a278571bdfaa91fb9ac50cde7664d2809810a2d7c2176364cc8",
            "ev:bc7beb3cc00068e44858d7d7ed5334b4432368715183e51d32c86e960873c130"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Part III examination instructions require recording medication status, time since the last levodopa dose, and clinical ON/OFF state; these conditions matter when interpreting repeated motor examinations. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.movementdisorders.org/MDS-Files1/PDFs/Rating-Scales/MDS-UPDRS_English_FINAL.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2b92c65ebf3e676f63fcb3ec39f87dfd9c63ef4a770ce27bb84117d0a665b9f6",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1cd815b68511cd4b92fcdbbaf0683df14744e1b26270ee981603f7ebd4e8e3d3",
            "ev:cee1957d5f897f86405943e72979e36b8a8d4793aae8ddfba649c6d712d8edb1"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6851993/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In a study of the MDS-UPDRS Motor Examination (Part III) with 728 paired investigations of 260 patients, minimal clinically important difference estimates were asymmetric: −3.25 points for minimal clinically pertinent improvement and +4.63 for worsening, using clinician global-impression anchors and distribution methods. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26578041/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:04bd5ecec24b392fda9cf99bc94d25224851d3c92bd799516ee68ca0b06c4256",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:c69a8b02c456a51ec738450db27e0930774c9651be420de357a17830f510c33d"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A 2017 study of paired investigations from 365 patients estimated minimal meaningful changes in Part I of more than 2.64 points improvement or 2.45 worsening, and Part II of 3.05 improvement or 2.51 deterioration; these are study estimates for the specified parts. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28218413/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a5e68de7018aba83cf1c4eab33aaa1fa44d78ac76afae23b10f8ef61531c9308",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0003643c14165733f0767b85adcdaa704dac2e4a9eb803c5ba1f5e32f52b83e3",
            "ev:129fc7e0e4e8f2bb24365c925cf1fb042bc7bc9405b8959321d0443e143f8a89",
            "ev:e7ea93ede909cac0ad215417a30d5c277ca48968c6536773e61a616d6761f48a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Original UPDRS and MDS-UPDRS scores should not be treated as interchangeable: a 2012 calibration study supported conversion formulas for Parts II and III, but did not achieve concordance for Parts I and IV. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22886777/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4a449dce4f07b5b6df652ef657ac03388a6a5b8cb208c69e9231f2fabd7217d3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0117f2fa4b3028c70a955a1a6e88846802ce6c6c09d270cd7f25b8f01d9dd878",
            "ev:03e5a7eaf4b7c10116a3ae20bdca6c4b60b7079e05a5dcd32f99b6a3094666c5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The MDS Non-Motor Rating Scale (MDS-NMS) consists of 13 domains plus a subscale for non-motor fluctuations and is rater-administered; in its initial multicenter validation study, internal consistency was acceptable (average Cronbach's alpha 0.66 and 0.84 for the scale total and the non-motor fluctuations total), interrater reliability was excellent (intraclass correlation coefficient >0.95) and test-retest intraclass correlation was 0.84 for the scale total. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31571279/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a55ea963163139668d41a69db4c8571839438a35d951830020d8d98cb545c034",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2c3612b78ef34cea711259f93e36966547f601ca4bb36994df4f49220fcd59a3",
            "ev:fa4b1e4e6ac871e1c961eeea45370eb769f5b9202aac74511c412e34d0b7371e"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A 2019 PPMI analysis of 423 de novo patients estimated within-subject reliability of one-year change scores: Part II and Part III OFF each reached 0.50. Its authors cautioned that change scores contained substantial error variance. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6851993/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:bc5459e4424ea2b309f9b7bd3b6b21ccaf6a254dff24ba427b8fc1488b837437",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1ba451047d761865f9db6c4c2025149d53e66f7e22d43cc16e5edd560830f698",
            "ev:2febdb8ae8270c337205487f8d0ec5e87bc719278c175c0bce0c9629ea67771e",
            "ev:345d99a264a52e696b62a3c5992a7c0175b53a6612fb71e3ff8a5e2fd40ef273",
            "ev:a10255b93a7ab45c1adb52324e09e7db86178e9c06af559a8c294c876cfe610d",
            "ev:b697c41663d4bf0d345052d2f20b5ac1dde8b58e4fb1383faa60c68294d46546"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Early-disease sensitivity requires caution: a Rasch analysis found floor effects and disordered response thresholds in Parts II and III; a separate comparison did not support greater sensitivity of MDS-UPDRS than UPDRS for mild motor severity in de novo PD. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6647182/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fdb4eb2250c46f37bbc8b9ac70a9566a60c529a935c7af4cfc1030738c91d9ff",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:19797b896a940c658f9182c7869110f2f88a37bc31e08f76e326427a2fb33b02",
            "ev:6d2afd5178c6638d7b9316264990ed174bc1ab2ef507a81f872ae5f64e4a4490",
            "ev:7a014a09735fd586bc0917c113d67a546b80ecb6235bdcef31e76e58ed9151a9"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://movementdisorders.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/mdc3.13329"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The MDS website describes the MDS-UPDRS as a revision of the original Unified Parkinson's Disease Rating Scale (developed in the 1980s) that addresses problematic areas of the original scale identified by an MDS review task force; it was developed to evaluate non-motor and motor experiences of daily living and motor complications, includes a motor evaluation, and can be used in clinical settings and in research. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.movementdisorders.org/MDS/MDS-Rating-Scales/MDS-Unified-Parkinsons-Disease-Rating-Scale-MDS-UPDRS.htm",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5286fe4944ca762ef210cee5328131217e786a3a1c78332dc2016c04931becad",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1b3480e4af9d3420b86c8370261cc2455c6eee502e259be7c5f9d4ad4ce2e2f4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The PDQ-39 is a short 39-item quality-of-life questionnaire for Parkinson's disease whose data can be presented in profile form or as a single index; a briefer derived measure (PDQ-8) also exists. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9617716/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:508c6d05e8f4a2971895e0795ab92010a6a9df5713d5c15910d1ce514d490d1e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5a892eb9a0970dc50227fb1946ca58a9f56ef49d0d03987200b0d12f65a5e7fe"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
